Z||000000||rockcrawl||01-28-2001||10:20 PM||||Check out this site and download the video of a cummins diesel doing a wild smokey figure 8 burnout on public streets. It is the funniest thing I've seen in a while. <A HREF="http://www.bd-power.com/ram/1000.php" TARGET=_blank>http://www.bd-power.com/ram/1000.php</A>  Somehow they've managed to squeeze out 1000 ft/lb of torque at the wheels.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||zeusrekning||01-29-2001||06:46 PM||||They showed that video on crank and chrome this week end.Added an exhaust brake, some kinda computer or chip that plugged into the fuel pump and increased tranny line pressure.Said gain about 100 hp and over 100lb of torque don't remember the exact number but dosent seem like any where near 1000||||reg||1
Z||000002||rockcrawl||01-29-2001||08:57 PM||||Yeah, that's where I saw it first, on Crank&Chrome. The truck in the video appears to be owned by BD Performance so I'm sure it's worked over pretty well. They claim (on the website) that it puts 1000 ft/lb to the wheels. But even the added 100 hp just by plugging in the computer mod is pretty impressive.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
